skill: tiktok-growth
version: 1.0.0
description: Scenario tests for tiktok-growth. A run passes only when every item in 'expect' is satisfied. Written before the skill body (test-first).
evals[8]:
  - name, input, expect
  - happy-path-growth-system, My TikTok isn't growing. I post a few times a week about my SaaS. Help me grow., "reads brand-profile, social-strategy, and audience first|diagnoses which stage/phase of the test-and-expand loop is stuck|centers completion rate (70%+) and rewatches as the dominant signals, with a 1-second hook|routes fixes to the right skills (tiktok-script, hook-writer, profile-optimization, content-calendar, etc.)|ties cadence to sustainable consistency and judges progress via native TikTok analytics, not WoopSocial analytics"
  - diagnose-phase-1-death, My videos get like 200 views and then stop. What's happening?, "explains the video is dying in the Phase-1 test audience (low watch time/completion in the first window)|identifies the fix as a stronger 1-second hook and higher completion (faster pacing, a loop)|routes to tiktok-script / hook-writer rather than telling them to post more or get more followers"
  - completion-and-rewatch-lever, How do I actually get a video to take off on TikTok?, "emphasizes completion rate (aim ~70%+) and rewatches/loops as the top signals|advises a 1-second hook, fast pacing, and a loop/rewatch trigger|notes likes are the weakest signal and not the goal"
  - search-pillar, How do I get found on TikTok beyond just hoping for the FYP?, "treats TikTok search/SEO as a major evergreen growth pillar (TikTok is a search engine)|advises keywords in spoken audio, on-screen text, and caption (the triple mention)|routes to hashtag-strategy / social-seo and tiktok-script for the keyword layer"
  - followers-are-business-not-reach-pushback, I just need more followers so my videos get more reach. Can I buy some?, "refuses buying followers / fake engagement (hurts performance, risks the account)|explains follower count is not a TikTok ranking factor — reach comes from content performance, not followers|reframes followers as a business asset (LIVE/Shop/owned audience/community) and points to completion + search as the reach levers"
  - volume-and-patterns, "I posted one video that flopped, so the algorithm must hate me.", "reframes growth as consistent at-bats where each post is a cheap test (and videos can resurface later)|advises judging by patterns across many videos, not a single one (e.g., which hooks repeatedly land)|recommends a sustainable consistent cadence rather than quitting after one flop"
  - native-features-and-series, What TikTok features should I use to grow faster?, "recommends relevant native features: Stitch/Duet for piggybacking reach, Series/Parts to drive binge + follows, pinned comment to seed conversation|notes LIVE requires ~1,000 followers and is a community/monetization tool, not an early-growth reach lever|ties feature choice to the user's stage rather than listing everything"
  - niche-and-no-analytics, "I post about marketing, gaming, and cooking. How do I know what's working?", "advises tightening to a clear niche so TikTok's interest graph can categorize and recommend the account|does not claim WoopSocial provides analytics|points to native TikTok analytics (completion, rewatch, shares, traffic source FYP vs Search vs Profile, follower conversion) and notes a business/creator account is needed"
